sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant EA as External assistant
    participant MCP as MCP endpoint
    participant TL as Tool layer
    participant TC as Tenant AI control
    participant GS as Interceptor and guardrails
    participant DS as Draft store
    participant H as Named human in the product
    participant TW as Target write path
    participant AU as India audit log
    EA->>MCP: Write tool call with an idempotency key, under a user grant
    MCP->>TL: Resolves the human principal behind the grant
    TL->>TC: Reads external write access and per-tool disablement for this client
    TC-->>TL: Write tier on for this client, tool not disabled
    TL->>TL: Maps the tool to its registered use case, checks the principal scope and the key
    alt Same key and same arguments inside the window
        TL-->>MCP: Returns the first call's draft id, nothing new staged
    else Same key with different arguments
        TL-->>MCP: Conflict, nothing staged
    else New key
        TL->>GS: Staged content runs the same checks as a model-written draft
        GS-->>TL: Pass only if every figure is a bound engine value
        TL->>DS: Draft created in PRESENTED with the principal as requester
        TL-->>MCP: Draft id and PRESENTED, no sign-off affordance
        MCP-->>EA: A named person must sign this off in the product
        DS->>H: In-product notification showing the whole draft
        H->>DS: Signs off from an interactive session
        DS->>TW: Applied through the target's own write path, after any checker
        TW->>AU: One audit event joining the draft id and the tool call id
    end
    TL->>AU: Every tool call row, allowed or refused
